INT. MINIVAN - CAR WASH TUNNEL - DAY

Soap foam pours down the windshield. Giant blue brushes slap the roof. The conveyor drags the van forward at a crawl.

GUS PAPADAKIS (40s, driver, tie loosened) grips the wheel though he doesn't have to. In the passenger seat, MIRABEL (10, glittery backpack, face pressed to the glass) watches the brushes. In the back, TOBIAH (7, missing teeth, a plastic dinosaur in each fist) bounces. Beside him, NANA ZOFIA (80s, handbag on her lap, church hat pinned in place) watches the foam as if it were a sermon.

GUS
Everybody seat belts?

MIRABEL
Yes.

TOBIAH
Yes!

NANA ZOFIA
I have been wearing seat belts since before you were a thought.

GUS
(muttering)
Thank you, Mama.

A giant brush slams the windshield. Mirabel shrieks. Tobiah shrieks louder, delighted. Nana Zofia clutches her handbag and pulls her hat down over her ears.

MIRABEL
Dad, you said it wasn't scary!

GUS
It's not scary.

MIRABEL
It's literally attacking us!

TOBIAH
(to his dinosaurs)
Stegosaurus, hold on. Hold on, T. rex.

The conveyor jerks. The van lurches. Gus slams the brake, and everything stops, foam sliding down the windows, brushes humming.

GUS
(to himself)
Don't panic. Don't panic.

Mirabel and Tobiah grab each other. Nana Zofia grabs Gus by the shoulder, hard. All three of them stare through the foam at the red light ahead.

NANA ZOFIA
Auguste. What did you do?

GUS
I didn't do anything.

NANA ZOFIA
You pressed the button.

GUS
Which button?

MIRABEL
The one that says "Do Not Press."

Silence. The brushes spin down. The foam thins. Water ticks off the roof. Through the windshield they see the exit, ten feet away, a rectangle of white daylight.

TOBIAH
Are we dead?

GUS
We're in a car wash.

TOBIAH
Is it heaven?

NANA ZOFIA
(dry)
If it were heaven, there would be no tip jar.

Gus starts to laugh, then Mirabel, then Tobiah. Nana Zofia holds out for another three seconds, and then breaks.

The conveyor restarts. The van rolls out into the sun, shining.
